# =====================================================================
# Monorepo .gitignore — AI-Powered Loan Risk & Recommendation System
# Covers four modules (see ARCHITECTURE.md, CURRENCY_FEATURE.md):
#   finance-frontend/         React + Vite
#   finance-backend/          Node + Express + MySQL
#   loan-risk-model/          Python + FastAPI + XGBoost
#   currency-forecast-model/  Python + FastAPI (LSTM/XGBoost/GARCH/IsoForest)
# =====================================================================

# ---------- Secrets / environment ----------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env

# ---------- OS / editor ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---------- Logs ----------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# =====================================================================
# Node  (finance-frontend + finance-backend)
# =====================================================================
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
*.local
coverage/

# Uploaded user files — keep the folder in git, ignore uploaded content
finance-backend/uploads/profile/*
!finance-backend/uploads/profile/.gitkeep

# FX compliance documents. Deliberately NOT under uploads/, which src/app.js
# serves as unauthenticated static — these are identity/purpose evidence and
# are only readable via the ownership-checked download route.
finance-backend/secure-uploads/fx-documents/*
!finance-backend/secure-uploads/fx-documents/.gitkeep

# Loan-supporting documents (identity, payslip, bank statement) — same
# reasoning as fx-documents above: only readable via the ownership-checked
# download route in loan.controller.js, never served statically.
finance-backend/secure-uploads/loan-documents/*
!finance-backend/secure-uploads/loan-documents/.gitkeep

# =====================================================================
# Python  (loan-risk-model)
# =====================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
venv/
.venv/
loan-risk-model/env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---------- ML data & artifacts (large + reproducible) ----------
# Dataset is regenerated with:  python -m src.data_generator
loan-risk-model/data/*.csv
loan-risk-model/data/*.parquet
# Model + preprocessor are retrained with:  python -m src.model_utils
# NOTE: while these are ignored, a fresh clone must retrain before the API
# will start. To ship a ready-to-run model instead, comment out the next
# two lines (the .joblib files are only ~8 MB).
loan-risk-model/model_artifacts/*.joblib
loan-risk-model/model_artifacts/*.pkl
# evaluation_report.txt stays tracked (small, useful for history).

# =====================================================================
# Python  (currency-forecast-model)
# =====================================================================
# Raw H.10 pulls and processed feature sets are reproducible from
# src/data_fetcher.py / src/feature_engineering.py — keep folders via
# .gitkeep, ignore their contents.
currency-forecast-model/data/raw/*
!currency-forecast-model/data/raw/.gitkeep
currency-forecast-model/data/processed/*
!currency-forecast-model/data/processed/.gitkeep
# Side-by-side builds from prepare_data.py --processed-dir (e.g. the
# FRED-refreshed dataset) are equally reproducible.
currency-forecast-model/data/processed_*/
# Trained artifacts are reproducible via training/train_*.py.
#currency-forecast-model/models/*
!currency-forecast-model/models/.gitkeep

# ---------- Local working doc (not committed) ----------
GUIDANCE.md
